WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.910
In 1911, the Supreme Court ordered
Standard Oil to be broken up.

2
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.950
One giant firm became
34 separate companies.

3
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.760
Today, the Department of
Justice and the Federal Trade

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.120
Commission still watch for price
fixing and for risky mergers.

5
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.620
So when should the government step in,

6
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.180
and when should it leave big firms alone?

7
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.670
In this mission, you'll sort the three
kinds of behavior antitrust law targets.

8
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.920
Then you'll meet the laws
behind antitrust policy,

9
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.050
starting in 1890.

10
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.650
Your mission: find out when
antitrust policy should step

11
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.440
in to protect competition.
